    "title": "Solar lights installed around Mesa Verde Park - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Jordan Honeycutt No media credit provided. ,\n52 minutes ago\nALBUQUERQUE, N.M. (KRQE) – A neighborhood in Albuquerque’s International District just got a little brighter. Over the last two weeks, the city installed five new solar lights around Mesa Verde Park, located near Pennsylvania Blvd. and Marquette Ave. The Director of the City of Albuquerque’s Municipal Development said neighbors have asked for more lights there, and solar lights are considered low maintenance.\nBernalillo County redeveloping property in North Valley to be the future home of ASL Academy and more The city is putting in nearly 200 of them along Central Ave. from Louisiana Blvd. to Juan Tabo Blvd.\nCopyright 2025 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to KRQE NEWS 13 - Breaking News, Albuquerque News, New Mexico News, Weather, and Videos.",
